{#
calendar/_happening_soon.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
"Happening Soon": everything expected within the fortnight — what plMail read
out of mail and what the owner put in the calendar themselves — loaded into the
app's body-level modal frame.

Accepts:
  rows  list<HappeningSoonRow> — already windowed, ordered, COLLAPSED and capped
        by HappeningSoonReader; this template windows nothing, sorts nothing and
        merges nothing

One meeting is one row. A meeting that reached plMail twice — extracted from its
invitation onto the account's calendar, mirrored from the provider onto a Remote
one — is one HappeningSoonRow carrying both, exactly as the grid draws it as one
chip. Where it is more than one row of the database, the icon tile wears the
same conic-gradient dot _event_chip wears and names the calendars in its title,
because a list that silently merges is indistinguishable from a list that lost
something.

Four things per row, and each earns its place. The ICON, off the row rather than
straight off the enum, so a fortnight can be read by shape before it is read by
word — a plane among boxes is found without reading anything, and an event
nobody extracted gets a plain calendar mark rather than a hole in the column.
WHEN, because that is the question. WHAT. And WHICH MESSAGE it came from, where
there is one: an extracted row is a guess a program made about somebody's mail,
and "why is this on my calendar?" has to be answerable in one click or the guess
is unfalsifiable. That link is the whole reason extracted events are marked as
extracted, and its absence on a hand-made row is the correct answer — nothing
made that one but the person reading it.

The provenance link carries `data-turbo-frame="_top"`. Without it Turbo reads a
link inside a <turbo-frame> as a navigation OF that frame, so clicking "from
this email" would load the whole mailbox page into the dialog and leave the user
inside a modal with no way back to their mail. The event editor's form documents
the same trap from the other direction.

A row whose message is gone renders without the link rather than with a dead
one. An event keeps its kind after the mail behind it is expunged
provider-side, and a link to a message that is not there is worse than no link.

The empty state is written as an answer, not as an absence. "Nothing coming up"
plus a line saying what would appear here — a panel that opens on blank space
reads as a panel that failed to load, and this one is empty for most people on
most days, which is the normal case and must not look like a fault.
#}

{% set rows = rows|default([]) %}

<turbo-frame id="modal" class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col">

    {% if rows is empty %}
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-2 px-6 pb-8 pt-4 text-center">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar-check text-2xl text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink">{{ 'calendar.soon.empty'|trans }}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint max-w-xs">{{ 'calendar.soon.empty_hint'|trans }}</p>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <ul class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto px-6 pb-5 divide-y divide-line">
            {% for row in rows %}
                {# Both fall back rather than rendering empty: a booking mail
                   with no Subject: header is rare and a blank line where the
                   provenance should be reads as a bug. #}
                {% set row_title = row.event.title ?: 'calendar.soon.untitled'|trans %}
                {% set row_from = 'calendar.soon.from'|trans({
                    '%subject%': row.source ? (row.source.subject ?: 'calendar.soon.untitled'|trans) : '',
                }) %}

                {# Equal slices in the members' order, the same construction and
                   the same reading as the merged chip's dot — one affordance
                   learned once. Built only for a merged row: a cluster of one
                   has a single calendar and a plain coloured dot would add a
                   mark to every line for no information. #}
                {% if row.cluster.isMerged %}
                    {% set slices = [] %}
                    {% for color in row.cluster.colors %}
                        {% set slices = slices|merge([
                            color
                                ~ ' ' ~ (loop.index0 * 100 / row.cluster.colors|length)|round(3) ~ '%'
                                ~ ' ' ~ (loop.index * 100 / row.cluster.colors|length)|round(3) ~ '%',
                        ]) %}
                    {% endfor %}
                    {% set row_on = 'calendar.chip.on_calendars'|trans({
                        '%calendars%': row.cluster.calendarNames|join(', '),
                    }) %}
                {% endif %}

                <li class="flex items-start gap-3 py-3">

                    {# The icon carries the kind's name as text for anyone who
                       cannot see it, so the row still says "Flight" rather than
                       leaving the shape to do all the work. #}
                    <span class="relative mt-0.5 flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center
                                 rounded-lg bg-sunken text-ink-muted">
                        <i class="{{ row.icon }} text-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i>

                        {% if row.cluster.isMerged %}
                            <span class="absolute -right-0.5 -top-0.5 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full
                                         ring-2 ring-surface"
                                  style="background: conic-gradient({{ slices|join(', ') }})"
                                  title="{{ row_on }}"></span>
                            <span class="sr-only">{{ row_on }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </span>

                    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                        <p class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-ink" title="{{ row_title }}">
                            {{ row_title }}
                        </p>

                        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-ink-muted">
                            <span class="sr-only">{{ row.transKey|trans }} · </span>
                            {# An all-day row is floating — a wall date at
                               midnight with no zone — so `false` keeps it in
                               its own, and the reader's clock does not move it
                               onto the day before. #}
                            {{ row.startsAt|date('D, j M', row.event.isAllDay ? false : null) }}
                            {%- if not row.event.isAllDay %} · {{ row.startsAt|date(clock.time) }}{% endif %}
                        </p>

                        {% if row.source is not null %}
                            <a href="{{ path('app_mail_message', { id: row.source.id }) }}"
                               data-turbo-frame="_top"
                               class="mt-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center gap-1.5
                                      text-xs text-ink-faint hover:text-accent hover:underline"
                               title="{{ row_from }}">
                                <i class="fa-regular fa-envelope text-[10px] shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                <span class="truncate">{{ row_from }}</span>
                            </a>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% endif %}

</turbo-frame>
